<p>Venezuela said it deported Colombian-born businessman and former industry minister Alex Saab to the United States on May 16 to face criminal proceedings, after years in which Nicolás Maduro&#x27;s government had defended him. Venezuela&#x27;s SAIME migration authority said it acted under immigration law because Saab, whom it identified as Colombian, was allegedly involved in various crimes in the United States. Saab, 54, was detained in Cape Verde in 2020, extradited to the United States in 2021 and granted clemency by President Joe Biden in 2023 as part of a prisoner exchange before returning to Venezuela. Several sources said the handover came after Maduro&#x27;s January capture by U.S. forces and the rise of acting President Delcy Rodríguez, whose government removed Saab from office and has increased cooperation with U.S. law enforcement.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/aUQEXD-HuOSRBxB1V5i8rPZw_mxAYeBvXChUlUYfwXcHHztL_mI6dD42ClXiofWrfNJcxoV2-KCChJKw6yDbxcUiqM5nRR8i_ADXagUDU6GFV2M_PrXAjtMp1zgkiLyN7JIfe8PBb_D_JBZ0R0sQO0oEaDg36-BOTHw2CGsIaEmxZoi01qBe7HvEdiNTNBEc' alt='Alex Saab, center, in Caracas, Venezuela, in 2023, was once among key allies of the deposed Venezuelan president, Nicolás Maduro.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Miami arrival: EFE reported Saab landed at Opa-locka airport in Miami-Dade County at sunset, escorted by federal agents including DEA personnel.</li><li>New indictment: U.S. prosecutors filed a new corruption indictment in Miami in January, according to El Financiero and Efecto Cocuyo, after earlier proceedings had ended with Saab&#x27;s 2023 clemency.</li><li>February detention: The New York Times reported that Rodríguez&#x27;s government detained Saab in early February at Washington&#x27;s request before the May handover.</li><li>Potential evidence: Some sources said investigators believe Saab could provide information relevant to cases against Maduro and his wife, Cilia Flores, who deny the charges they face in New York.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Venezuelan migration authority SAIME: SAIME&#x27;s statement used the phrase &#x27;public, notorious and communicational&#x27; to describe Saab&#x27;s alleged U.S. offenses and cited an administrative migration rationale. (<a href='http://caribbeannews.net/news/279056333/venezuela-deports-nicolas-maduro-ally-alex-saab-amid-us-criminal-investigations'>Caribbean News</a>)</li><li>Venezuelan opposition figures: Opposition figures welcomed the handover after weeks in which Saab&#x27;s whereabouts had been unclear. (<a href='https://albertonews.com/internacionales/la-oposicion-venezolana-celebro-la-deportacion-de-alex-saab-puede-convertirse-en-uno-de-los-testigos-mas-importantes-en-el-caso-maduro/'>AlbertoNews</a>)</li><li>U.S. prosecutors: U.S. prosecutors have accused Saab of enriching himself through lucrative Venezuelan government contracts. Rodríguez&#x27;s government later removed him from office as part of a purge of Maduro-era power brokers. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/16/world/americas/venezuela-extradites-tycoon-alex-saab.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-deports-maduro-ally-alex-saab-to-us/a-77184876'>Venezuela deports Maduro ally Alex Saab to US</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/05/17/venezuela-hands-over-to-the-united-states-former-minister-and-maduro-frontman-alex-saab'>Venezuela hands over to the United States former minister and Maduro frontman Alex Saab</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/venezuela-says-it-deported-close-ally-of-maduro-to-face-criminal-proceedings-in-us/article70989495.ece'>Venezuela says it deported close ally of Maduro to face criminal proceedings in U.S.</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/venezuela-deports-maduro-ally-to-u-s-for-criminal-proceedings'>Venezuela deports Maduro ally to U.S. for criminal proceedin